---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | JSON Diff Checker';
const description =
  'Privacy Policy for JSON Diff Checker. All JSON comparison happens locally in your browser — we do not upload, store, or transmit the data you paste.';
---

<PageLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  eyebrow="Privacy policy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="September 6, 2026"
>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how JSON Diff Checker ("we", "our", "the tool") handles information when
    you use jsondiffchecker.com (the "Site"). We built this tool around a simple principle: the JSON data
    you compare is yours, and it never leaves your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Data you paste or upload</h2>
  <p>
    All parsing, validation, and comparison of JSON happens locally in your browser using client-side
    JavaScript. We do not have a backend server that receives, stores, logs, or processes the content you
    paste, upload, or load into the tool. If you load JSON from a URL you provide, that request is made
    directly from your browser to the URL you specify — we do not proxy or intercept it.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    We use your browser's local storage only to remember your theme preference (light or dark mode). This
    information stays on your device and is not transmitted to us or any third party.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The Site does not load third-party analytics scripts, advertising tags, or tracking pixels. You can
    verify this by opening your browser's developer tools and inspecting the Network tab while using the
    tool.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    The Site may link to third-party resources, such as RFC specifications. We are not responsible for the
    privacy practices of external websites, and we encourage you to review their respective privacy
    policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information
    from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an
    updated "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please visit our <a href="/contact-us">Contact Us</a> page.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
